{
  "name": "CH-00 Client Hunt - Discover from open data",
  "settings": {
    "executionOrder": "v1",
    "timezone": "Asia/Karachi"
  },
  "active": false,
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "rule": {
          "interval": [
            {
              "field": "hours",
              "hoursInterval": 6
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "ch00-trigger-schedule",
      "name": "Every 6 hours",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        -780,
        200
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {},
      "id": "ch00-trigger-manual",
      "name": "Run manually",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.manualTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -780,
        380
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "f1",
              "name": "per_target_per_run",
              "value": 10,
              "type": "number"
            },
            {
              "id": "f2",
              "name": "telegram_chat_id",
              "value": "__ENV:TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID__",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "q3",
              "name": "stop_when_pending_above",
              "value": 150,
              "type": "number"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "ch00-config",
      "name": "Config",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3.4,
      "position": [
        -560,
        290
      ],
      "notes": "per_target_per_run x 4 runs a day x enabled targets = leads a day. The real limit is downstream: CH-02 verifies about 720 a day, and every lead costs one or two Serper searches from the free 2,500."
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "operation": "executeQuery",
        "query": {
          "$sql": "insert-open-data-leads.sql"
        },
        "options": {
          "queryReplacement": "={{ [$('Config').first().json.per_target_per_run, $('Config').first().json.stop_when_pending_above] }}"
        }
      },
      "id": "ch00-insert",
      "name": "Take new leads from open data",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.postgres",
      "typeVersion": 2.5,
      "position": [
        -340,
        290
      ],
      "executeOnce": true,
      "credentials": {
        "postgres": {
          "name": "Client Hunt DB"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": {
          "$snippet": "ch00-summary.js"
        }
      },
      "id": "ch00-summary",
      "name": "What did we add?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        -120,
        290
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## CH-00 \u2014 Discover from open data\n\nFree discovery. Takes leads from the Overture places already loaded for each enabled target's city: in the niche's categories (`niche_categories`), with a phone, holding no website, not closed, and not already a business here.\n\nThey are stored `PENDING` with source `overture`, and CH-02 verifies them exactly like an Apify lead - search, domain probes, PageSpeed. Stage B is kept from matching a lead against its own Overture record, so the dataset never vouches for itself.\n\nOnly cities with reference data are used (Oslo and Dubai today). Load another with `tools/load_reference_data.py`.\n\nCosts nothing to run. The real limits are CH-02's pace and Serper's free search credits.",
        "height": 440,
        "width": 560,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "ch00-sticky",
      "name": "What this is",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1420,
        100
      ]
    }
  ],
  "connections": {
    "Every 6 hours": {
